    "theme": {
        "$comment": "The tabloid register's overlay: mode light opens the site on its native newsprint (the appearance toggle still swaps to the night-desk dark variant), and the preset's fire-engine red rides as the project brand so app-side surfaces (the code-gated proofing room's chrome and controls) wear the same red as the pages instead of the kernel default blue. Brand values match the tabloid preset's own light/dark accents — the marketing pages resolve brand over preset accent, so keeping them identical re-brands the app without shifting the pages. navigation pins the centered nameplate (the paper's flag over a ruled band of section links), matching editionShell.ts — a declared theme variant outranks the shell prop.",
        "mode": "light",
        "brand": {
            "primary": "#d0161e",
            "primaryDark": "#f0333a"
        },
        "navigation": {
            "variant": "centered"
        }
    },
    "landing": {
        "$comment": "Doc-aware pack pages: routes maps each pack route to the page id its config merges under (web/app/src/View/WeddingEdition/WeddingEditionPage.tsx, useSitePageConfig). pages seeds each page's layout skeleton — ids and variants match editionLanding.ts; the platform's structural editor edits these. Roll interiors (/weddings?roll=<slug>) merge under roll-<slug> and are deliberately unseeded, so adding a roll is a content edit. style must ride the overlay: the compose merge keeps the kernel document's root style otherwise, and applySitePageDocument makes the document preset outrank every page's pinned one. The preset is tabloid (Anton banner caps, serif columns, newsprint, black column rules, fire-engine red, halftone-screened photographs) — the wedding as the morning-after front page.",
        "style": {
            "preset": "tabloid"
        },
